From: xcentaurix
Subject: [PATCH] GStreamer: use bounded buffering (not unbounded "download" mode) for progressive downloads

A large (multi-GiB) progressive MP4 could silently never start playing: no error, no picture, forever. Root cause was two cooperating
pieces of WebKit's own GStreamer pipeline setup, both requesting unbounded "download" mode for any playing (non-blob, non-MediaSource,
non-MediaStream) URL once its size is known:

 - MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::configureElement() set urisourcebin's "download" property to TRUE for such URLs (only blob URIs got the
   safer, bounded "ring-buffer-max-size" instead).
 - MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::updateDownloadBufferingFlag() independently (and redundantly) set playbin's own GST_PLAY_FLAG_DOWNLOAD bit
   whenever preload="auto" and disk caching wasn't disabled - overriding whatever configureElement() had set on the element directly.

"download" mode makes GStreamer's downloadbuffer element eagerly download the *entire* resource to disk, sequentially, from the start,
regardless of what the demuxer currently needs - and, for a large file, it also switches the demuxer to PULL scheduling against that
(still-filling) buffer. For qtdemux specifically, this means its own small, one-shot pull-mode probe reads (e.g. the read-past-end-of-file
check it does right after parsing a fast-start moov, to confirm there's nothing more to scan) share the same HTTP source element and its
mutex with downloadbuffer's own continuous, eager prefetch loop. The probe can lose that race - get pre-empted before receiving any data -
for tens of seconds on a real multi-GiB file, during which nothing plays and nothing errors: qtdemux's header-scan loop only reaches its
"switch to MOVIE state" transition once its own probe finally succeeds, which can take as long as the eager prefetch takes to get out of
its way.

Fix: never request unbounded "download" mode. Use the same bounded ring buffer already used for blob URIs for every progressive URL (a
little larger, since a remote resource benefits from more look-ahead/look-behind headroom than an already-local blob), and never set
GST_PLAY_FLAG_DOWNLOAD at all. Removing the "keep downloading forever, regardless of demand" behavior removes the starvation itself, not
just one symptom of it - and, as a side effect for progressive MP4 specifically, lets qtdemux fall back to its simpler push-mode/adapter
state machine (which transitions to MOVIE state right after parsing moov, without needing to scan to the true end of file first) instead
of pull-mode scheduling against a downloadbuffer.

Reproduced and verified with a synthetic sparse MP4 (real ~60 KB moov+small mdat prefix, sparse-extended mdat, trailing 68-byte free box,
served locally with a custom Range-supporting HTTP server) at both 5,014,522,180 bytes (matching a real failing ZDF film) and
4,238,966,549 bytes (matching a real working one): before this patch the failing-size file either silently stalled (qtdemux's header-scan
task starved for 89s behind an unrelated, unbounded prefetch in one run) or hit patch 0014's EOS-vs-error guard and errored out, depending
on timing; after this patch both sizes reach MOVIE state and start delivering frames within ~5 seconds, with no regression on the
already-working size.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
index 3455afc2..394b9876 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@ -2823,14 +2823,23 @@ void MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::configureElement(GstElement* element)
         configureUriDecodebin2(element);

     // In case of playbin3 with <video ... preload="auto">, instantiate downloadbuffer element,
-    // otherwise the playbin3 would instantiate a queue element instead. When playing blob URIs,
-    // configure urisourcebin to setup a ring buffer so that downstream demuxers operate in pull
-    // mode. Some demuxers (matroskademux) don't work as well in push mode.
+    // otherwise the playbin3 would instantiate a queue element instead. Configure urisourcebin to
+    // set up a (bounded) ring buffer so that downstream demuxers operate in pull mode. Some
+    // demuxers (matroskademux) don't work as well in push mode.
+    //
+    // This used to request unbounded "download" mode (keep the entire resource on disk forever)
+    // for any non-MediaSource/non-MediaStream progressive URL, blob or not. For a large (multi-GiB)
+    // progressive download that starves qtdemux's own small, pull-mode probe reads (e.g. its
+    // confirm-end-of-file check right after parsing a fast-start moov) against downloadbuffer's own
+    // eager, unbounded sequential prefetch of the whole file: both share the same underlying HTTP
+    // source element and its mutex, and the probe can lose that race for tens of seconds real files,
+    // during which nothing plays and nothing errors. A bounded ring buffer (matching the same size
+    // already used for blob URIs) removes the "keep downloading forever, regardless of demand"
+    // behavior entirely, which removes the starvation, not just its symptom (seen 2026-09-23 with
+    // >=4GiB progressive MP4 playback silently never starting).
     if (startsWith(name.span(), "urisourcebin"_s) && !m_isLegacyPlaybin && m_preload == MediaPlayer::Preload::Auto) {
-        if (isBlob)
-            g_object_set(element, "ring-buffer-max-size", 2 * MB, nullptr);
-        else if (!isMediaSource() && !isMediaStreamPlayer())
-            g_object_set(element, "download", TRUE, nullptr);
+        if (!isMediaSource() && !isMediaStreamPlayer())
+            g_object_set(element, "ring-buffer-max-size", (isBlob ? 2 : 8) * MB, nullptr);
     }

     // Collect processing time metrics for video decoders and converters.
@@ -3519,7 +3528,17 @@ void MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::updateDownloadBufferingFlag()
     bool diskCacheDisabled = isMediaDiskCacheDisabled();
     GST_DEBUG_OBJECT(pipeline(), "Media on-disk cache is %s", (diskCacheDisabled) ? "disabled" : "enabled");

-    bool shouldDownload = !m_isLiveStream.value_or(false) && m_preload == MediaPlayer::Preload::Auto && !diskCacheDisabled;
+    // GST_PLAY_FLAG_DOWNLOAD drives urisourcebin into unbounded "download" mode: the whole
+    // resource is kept on disk forever, downloaded eagerly and sequentially regardless of what
+    // the demuxer actually needs next. For a large (multi-GiB) progressive file this starves the
+    // demuxer's own small, pull-mode probe reads (e.g. qtdemux's confirm-end-of-file check right
+    // after parsing a fast-start moov) against that eager prefetch: both share the same underlying
+    // HTTP source element and its mutex, and the probe can lose that race for tens of seconds on a
+    // real file, during which nothing plays and nothing errors (seen 2026-09-23, >=4GiB progressive
+    // MP4). configureElement() already requests a bounded ring buffer on urisourcebin instead (same
+    // mechanism used for blob URIs) - never set this flag, so that bounded mode is what's actually
+    // used, not overridden by it.
+    bool shouldDownload = false;
     if (shouldDownload) {
         GST_INFO_OBJECT(pipeline(), "Enabling on-disk buffering");
         g_object_set(m_pipeline.get(), "flags", flags | flagDownload, nullptr);
